      "level": 3,
      "content": "D. Nervous Tissue"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mwt1o9o",
      "content": "Nervous tissue consists of neurons which transmit nerve impulses. It forms brain, spinal cord and nerves."
    },
    {
      "id": "0fqztyr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6.Additional Important Concepts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bz4r6tc",
      "content": "• Aerenchyma helps aquatic plants float."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "07ah4it",
      "content": "• Chlorenchyma performs photosynthesis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2ml140x",
      "content": "• Sclerenchyma cells are lignified."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z3e5x5t",
      "content": "• Xylem transports upward; Phloem transports in both directions."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Apical meristem increases length, while Lateral meristem (cambium) increases the girth/thickness of stems and roots.",
        "Sclerenchyma tissue cells are dead at maturity with thick lignified walls, providing mechanical strength (e.g., coconut husk).",
        "Xylem transport is unidirectional (water/minerals), while Phloem transport is bidirectional (food molecules).",
        "Blood is classified as a fluid connective tissue containing a liquid matrix called plasma."
      ],
      "id": "g28lek4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xjhitle",
      "content": "• Blood is fluid connective tissue."
    },
    {
      "id": "ay5of7k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7.Quick Revision Points"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tfqoxyi",
      "content": "1. Apical meristem increases plant length."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7tg7xrl",
      "content": "2. Sclerenchyma cells are dead at maturity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4o1rsqy",
      "content": "3. Xylem = Water transport; Phloem = Food transport."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7knq6iv",
      "content": "4. Cardiac muscle is only in heart."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fgskrxk",
      "content": "5. Blood is connective tissue."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zz9m25i",
      "content": "6. Tendon connects muscle to bone; Ligament connects bone to bone."
    }
  ],
